Dear Simon & list:

The video is very good on my FC2 install (Xp1000, Oxygen VX1 video card).  You
might want to try recompiling your x-server, or compiling and installing a
known good version of xfree86 from sources.

I get the same msgs:  ISP1020 i think refers to the Qlogic SCSI adapter chip.
I haven't had any problems with my hard drives or the on-board controller.

the missing updfstab.conf file may have some bearing on why my system did not
detect and install the floppy and CDrom drives.  I did that by editing
/etc/fstab and putting up some screen icons.  They seem to work but only root
can mount them!

The 7.2 redHat had its problems too, even though it was a corporate-sponsored
product.  FC2 is a labor of love by a very few dedicated individuals.  

If i figure out a workaround on the floppy nd CDrom drive situation I'll share it.

good luck

